WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.292
Begin with a field excitation.

2
00:00:02.292 --> 00:00:04.238
Start with the lifecycle scene.

3
00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:08.761
BHSM interprets particle structure through geometric organization.

4
00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:15.411
The field lines make an excitation visible, and the changing pattern introduces the idea of a localized mode.

5
00:00:15.411 --> 00:00:22.563
Follow this illustrative unstable excitation through propagation to a decay event, where daughter excitations appear.

6
00:00:22.563 --> 00:00:28.620
The animation supplies a visual sequence; its durations, paths and outgoing modes are schematic.

7
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.524
Use the pause button or select a phase to examine what changes.

8
00:00:32.524 --> 00:00:39.908
A physical decay calculation would also need the permitted interaction channels, conservation laws and a quantitative rate.

9
00:00:39.908 --> 00:00:43.117
Look for the moment when the parent becomes outgoing states.
